femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: carry more CSS and XHTML semantics through the styled event stream

This patch is NOT a single concern. It is the remainder of femto's changes
to src/css.rs and src/render_prep.rs after 0001-0003 are removed. The
changes below were made over time in the same functions (CssStyle,
parse_declarations, Styler::style_chapter_bytes_with,
resolve_context_style, element_ctx_from_start) and often on the same lines,
so they could not be separated mechanically. It needs to be split by hand
before any of it is proposed upstream. Contents:

 1. white-space: CSS property with inheritance; a streaming normaliser that
    shares collapse state across runs, entities and CDATA, keeps U+00A0,
    normalises CR/CRLF; <pre> defaults to pre and emits paragraph events;
    code/kbd/samp no longer imply preservation. Replaces
    normalize_plain_text_whitespace, which trimmed spaces at text-node
    boundaries and so removed spaces around inline elements.
 2. Anchors and links: Anchor, LinkStart, LinkEnd items from id/xml:id/name
    and <a href>; attribute values unescaped and capped at 4096 bytes.
 3. Notes: NoteReferenceStart for epub:type=noteref / role=doc-noteref
    links; NoteBodyStart/NoteBodyEnd around epub:type footnote/endnote and
    role doc-footnote/doc-endnote elements. Uses NsReader so the epub:type
    namespace is resolved rather than matched by prefix.
 4. Language: inherited lang / xml:lang on StyledRun (xml:lang wins; an
    empty value clears inheritance; malformed tags are an error).
 5. hyphens property with inheritance.
 6. text-align: start/end/inherit values; alignment taken from the
    containing block, not from inline elements.
 7. direction property and the XHTML dir attribute, block-level.
 8. tab-size property (number, px, em), em resolved at the declaring element.
 9. text-indent property (px, em, %), em resolved at the declaring element.
10. Lists: ListStart/ListEnd, list-style-type, ol type/start/reversed and
    li value/type, including a bounded pre-pass that counts items of
    reversed lists.
11. Images: width, height, min-*/max-* (px, %, auto/none) carried on
    StyledImage without inheritance; intrinsic-dimension back-fill is
    skipped when CSS dimensions or minima are present.
12. display property (inline/block/none/inherit), reported only through
    SourceElement.
13. Source tracking (RenderPrepOptions::track_source,
    Styler::with_source_tracking): TextSource token ranges and per-character
    offsets on runs, SourceElement items, StyledImage::source_offset. Used by
    femto to map reading positions to KOReader XPointers.

All of these add public fields or enum variants, so each is a breaking API
change for epub-stream. Tests for most of these are included in the same files.
femto's reasons are recorded in docs/dependencies.md, docs/typography.md,
docs/navigation.md and docs/koreader-sync.md.

